# Debug only: what the instrumentation test calls in the minified app under test.
#
# When the app under test is minified, the test APK leaves out every library the app already
# carries, and resolves those classes from the app at run time. R8 strips what the app itself never
# uses, so the test would crash before it starts (NoClassDefFoundError, "0 tests"). These rules keep
# exactly that set, and nothing the release lane proves: the Service, the server-side stubs and the
# contract messages still stand on the rules in main. Release builds never see this file.
#
# To re-derive it: build `:app:assembleDebug :app:assembleDebugAndroidTest -PminifyDebug`, then list
# the classes the test APK's dex references that neither APK defines.

# The Kotlin standard library the test libraries and the test reach for (kotlin.LazyKt and others).
-keep class kotlin.** { *; }

# The client side of the round trip: the app serves STREAM but never calls it.
-keep class io.grpc.binder.BinderChannelBuilder { *; }
-keep class io.grpc.ManagedChannel { *; }
-keep class io.grpc.Channel { *; }
-keep class io.grpc.CallOptions { *; }
-keep class com.binge.companion.contracts.stream.v1.StreamServiceGrpcKt$StreamServiceCoroutineStub { *; }

# Not kept, because no rule can: androidx.test's ViewCapture and WindowCapture refer to
# androidx.concurrent.futures.SuspendToFutureAdapter, which the concurrent-futures version this app
# resolves (1.1.0) does not have. The smoke test never captures a view, so the gap is never reached.
